  "reason": "The sole completed experiment (config_001, rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000) yields a low accuracy of 0.485, leaving substantial uncertainty about where the performance bottleneck lies. The most fundamental open question for a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether the image modality carries any independent predictive signal. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) cleanly tests this by isolating the image channel with a standard, well-understood encoder while removing RNA entirely. If image_only performs well, it confirms the image modality is informative and justifies investing subsequent experiments in multimodal fusion strategies. If it performs poorly, it indicates the image channel needs a stronger encoder (e.g., ViT) or that signal is primarily in the RNA modality, redirecting effort toward better RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt). This experiment maximizes information per trial because the answer bifurcates the entire search strategy: it determines whether to prioritize multimodal configurations or RNA-encoder improvements in the remaining budget."
}

